# Kept reasoning is restored in one pass over the conversation. KeptReasoning.restore (patch 0036) keyed each assistant
# tool step that came back without reasoning by a signature of the whole conversation before it, rebuilt for every
# step: each one re-encoded and hashed every earlier message, so a request cost the square of its length, in Python
# with the GIL held, before admission and outside the TTFT metric. An agent client that sends empty think blocks back
# bare (pi does) makes nearly every step a candidate: ~4-5 s a request at ~2,000 messages / ~400k tokens, with the
# engine loop and every other stream stopped meanwhile. _History keeps one running SHA-256 over the message shapes
# (each length-prefixed) and copies it at each step: one pass a request. The same keys cover the same history (role,
# stripped text, calls; no ids or reasoning), ids are still tried first, so the same steps are restored with the same
# reasoning; the key format is new, which only matters within one process. tools/kept_reasoning_check.py.

